Our ears perform no sound amplification.  As the article linked to by SP notes "The middle ear...acts as an amplifier of force"; it is the sound pressure that is increased, not the amplitude of the sound waves.  If one measured the sound wave amplitude outside the ear and again at the ear drum, the peaks and valleys of the sound waves would be equal or diminished.  But an instrument measuring pressure would show the increase as described.

